\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Model, pole EP and interaction evidence} (schematic). (a) The impurity $d$ couples through $W$ to the full radial SOC bath, which couples through $V_O$ to a remote fermionic level. Uniform phase rotation shifts the auxiliary energies by $\mp \Omega $. (b) The outgoing-sheet inverse kernel has a rank-one double zero; encircling it in two real controls exchanges the poles. (c) The finite-chain embedding and continuum KR saddle give method-specific interaction evidence. Here $\bar  \Gamma _0=W^2/4=0.0025$; at $U=0$ the retarded EP is independent of filling. The nearly occupied KR points remain charge fluctuating, and their constrained folds do not exclude nearby EPs. This panel is not a phase diagram.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{2}{\textbf {Model, pole EP and interaction evidence} (schematic). (a) The impurity $d$ couples through $W$ to the full radial SOC bath, which couples through $V_O$ to a remote fermionic level. Uniform phase rotation shifts the auxiliary energies by $\mp \Omega $. (b) The outgoing-sheet inverse kernel has a rank-one double zero; encircling it in two real controls exchanges the poles. (c) The finite-chain embedding and continuum KR saddle give method-specific interaction evidence. Here $\bar \Gamma _0=W^2/4=0.0025$; at $U=0$ the retarded EP is independent of filling. The nearly occupied KR points remain charge fluctuating, and their constrained folds do not exclude nearby EPs. This panel is not a phase diagram}{figure.1}{}}
