\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Finite-\(U\) continuation of the causal full-\(k\) pole EP.} (a) The branch-tracked local discriminant winds once clockwise around the origin on the interacting control ellipse at \(U=0.0025\). (b) The two nearby poles exchange after one circuit; open circles and filled squares mark the initial and final tracked labels, and the star marks Eq.~(\ref {eq:finiteU_fullk_center}). (c) The center of the finite-chain self-energy embedding varies smoothly from \(U=0\) to \(U/\bar  \Gamma _0=1\), where \(\bar  \Gamma _0=0.0025\). (d) The retuned impurity hybridization $W$ on the same path. The discriminant in (a) is normalized by its maximum modulus on the loop; the displacement scale in (b) is $10^{-4}$. Kept-space errors relative to the exact response on the same four shifted 12-site chains are tabulated in SM App.~C; they are not used to establish the winding. The separate $N=10\to 12$ common-contour gate is given by Eq.~(\ref {eq:finiteU_fullk_rouche}) and detailed in the Supplemental Material.}}{10}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:finiteU_fullk_exact}{{5}{10}{\textbf {Finite-\(U\) continuation of the causal full-\(k\) pole EP.} (a) The branch-tracked local discriminant winds once clockwise around the origin on the interacting control ellipse at \(U=0.0025\). (b) The two nearby poles exchange after one circuit; open circles and filled squares mark the initial and final tracked labels, and the star marks Eq.~(\ref {eq:finiteU_fullk_center}). (c) The center of the finite-chain self-energy embedding varies smoothly from \(U=0\) to \(U/\bar \Gamma _0=1\), where \(\bar \Gamma _0=0.0025\). (d) The retuned impurity hybridization $W$ on the same path. The discriminant in (a) is normalized by its maximum modulus on the loop; the displacement scale in (b) is $10^{-4}$. Kept-space errors relative to the exact response on the same four shifted 12-site chains are tabulated in SM App.~C; they are not used to establish the winding. The separate $N=10\to 12$ common-contour gate is given by Eq.~(\ref {eq:finiteU_fullk_rouche}) and detailed in the Supplemental Material}{figure.5}{}}
