\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Finite-\(U\) continuation of the full-\(k\) resonance EP with the continuum Kotliar--Ruckenstein saddle} ($T=0$). (a) Pole exchange at $U=0.2=80\bar  \Gamma _0$ ($\bar  \Gamma _0=0.0025$, $\mu =0$) on the control ellipse of Fig.~\ref {fig:full_k_certificate}, with the saddle re-solved at each of 128 points. Open circles and filled squares mark the initial and final poles; the colours exchange at each endpoint, and the star marks $z_{\rm  EP}$. (b) EP energy and gate on the branch with $W=0.10$ fixed and $(\epsilon _d,V_O)$ retuned; $U=0$ is Eq.~(\ref {eq:full_k_ep_solution}). (c) Retuned drive vertex and the traceless constraint field $|\vec  \Lambda _f|$ that moves the EP. (d) Impurity filling, double occupancy and smallest quasiparticle weight. (e) Shift of $W$ for the controls of Sec.~\ref {sec:finiteU}, $(\epsilon _d,W)$ at fixed $V_O$: ED on the four 12-site chains (the path of Eq.~(\ref {eq:finiteU_fullk_center})), KR with mesh-averaged inverse-kernel corrections on those chains, and KR on the continuum. Lines are the first-order Hartree--Fock rates with the chain and continuum density matrices. (f) Impurity filling at the EP for the same three calculations. Panels (e,f) compare method and bath dependence; the different ED and KR mesh averages are specified in SM App.~N. All KR results are mean-field saddle results. The filling-one EP and its constrained continuation are examined separately in Fig.~\ref {fig:KR_n1}.}}{11}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:finiteU_KR}{{6}{11}{\textbf {Finite-\(U\) continuation of the full-\(k\) resonance EP with the continuum Kotliar--Ruckenstein saddle} ($T=0$). (a) Pole exchange at $U=0.2=80\bar \Gamma _0$ ($\bar \Gamma _0=0.0025$, $\mu =0$) on the control ellipse of Fig.~\ref {fig:full_k_certificate}, with the saddle re-solved at each of 128 points. Open circles and filled squares mark the initial and final poles; the colours exchange at each endpoint, and the star marks $z_{\rm EP}$. (b) EP energy and gate on the branch with $W=0.10$ fixed and $(\epsilon _d,V_O)$ retuned; $U=0$ is Eq.~(\ref {eq:full_k_ep_solution}). (c) Retuned drive vertex and the traceless constraint field $|\vec \Lambda _f|$ that moves the EP. (d) Impurity filling, double occupancy and smallest quasiparticle weight. (e) Shift of $W$ for the controls of Sec.~\ref {sec:finiteU}, $(\epsilon _d,W)$ at fixed $V_O$: ED on the four 12-site chains (the path of Eq.~(\ref {eq:finiteU_fullk_center})), KR with mesh-averaged inverse-kernel corrections on those chains, and KR on the continuum. Lines are the first-order Hartree--Fock rates with the chain and continuum density matrices. (f) Impurity filling at the EP for the same three calculations. Panels (e,f) compare method and bath dependence; the different ED and KR mesh averages are specified in SM App.~N. All KR results are mean-field saddle results. The filling-one EP and its constrained continuation are examined separately in Fig.~\ref {fig:KR_n1}}{figure.6}{}}
