\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {An occupied, charge-fluctuating EP and its constrained continuation in the continuum KR saddle} ($T=0$). (a) Pole exchange at $\langle n_d\rangle =1$ and $U=0.0025=\bar  \Gamma _0$. The star marks $z_{\rm  EP}$; open circles and filled squares mark the initial and final poles. At the center, $D_d=0.229$ and $P_1=0.542$, so this is not a local-moment state. The loop keeps $\mu $ fixed and re-solves the saddle; its controls and numerical checks are given in SM App.~N. (b,c) EP branches constrained to $\langle n_d\rangle =1$, with $W=0.10$ or $V_O$ fixed, respectively. Circles continue in $U$; squares continue in the indicated control with $U$ as an unknown. Insets resolve local folds at $U_c/\bar  \Gamma _0=1.23$ and $3.18$. Here $\bar  \Gamma _0=0.0025$ is the fixed reference width, including in (c) where $W$ varies. These constrained turns do not exclude nearby EPs: releasing the filling constraint yields the verified KR point $U=0.0032$, $\langle n_d\rangle =0.98587$ (not plotted; SM App.~N). All results are mean-field saddle results.}}{12}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:KR_n1}{{7}{12}{\textbf {An occupied, charge-fluctuating EP and its constrained continuation in the continuum KR saddle} ($T=0$). (a) Pole exchange at $\langle n_d\rangle =1$ and $U=0.0025=\bar \Gamma _0$. The star marks $z_{\rm EP}$; open circles and filled squares mark the initial and final poles. At the center, $D_d=0.229$ and $P_1=0.542$, so this is not a local-moment state. The loop keeps $\mu $ fixed and re-solves the saddle; its controls and numerical checks are given in SM App.~N. (b,c) EP branches constrained to $\langle n_d\rangle =1$, with $W=0.10$ or $V_O$ fixed, respectively. Circles continue in $U$; squares continue in the indicated control with $U$ as an unknown. Insets resolve local folds at $U_c/\bar \Gamma _0=1.23$ and $3.18$. Here $\bar \Gamma _0=0.0025$ is the fixed reference width, including in (c) where $W$ varies. These constrained turns do not exclude nearby EPs: releasing the filling constraint yields the verified KR point $U=0.0032$, $\langle n_d\rangle =0.98587$ (not plotted; SM App.~N). All results are mean-field saddle results}{figure.7}{}}
